+# FAA ORB disk and DVD accession crosswalk
+
+November 9, 2026 Eastern · B129 / PD01 / PD07, recorder custody lead. The National Archives inventory for **237-06-0009** lists **N90-7**, an ORB disk described as a copy of **ORB #180**, and **N90-187**, a DVD described as a copy of **ORB #180**. The same comparison links 12 disk descriptions in agency box **16** to 12 DVD descriptions in box **18**. This gives separate item identifiers for requesting or identifying the underlying media and the records of its duplication. The date, operator, equipment and completeness of the copying remain open. [Accession inventory, physical p. 52](https://www.archives.gov/files/faa-inventory.pdf#page=52) · [DVD entries, physical pp. 56–57](https://www.archives.gov/files/faa-inventory.pdf#page=56) · [Exact finding-aid rows and source pins](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## Four records describe the same interval
+
+| Agency box and item | Medium | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 16 / **N90-6** | ORB Disk | ORB #96 - 0845 UTC - 1300 UTC (Original) |
+| 16 / **N90-7** | ORB Disk | ORB #180 - 0845 UTC - 1300 UTC (Copy) |
+| 18 / **N90-186** | DVD | Copy of ORB #96 - 0845 UTC - 1300 UTC |
+| 18 / **N90-187** | DVD | Copy of ORB #180 - 0845 UTC - 1300 UTC |
+
+The four rows preserve two disk numbers, two media types and an equal listed interval. A media manifest or comparison of authenticated images would test whether #180 is a faithful copy of #96 and whether each DVD reproduces the named disk. This review compared the descriptions. The finding aid supplies no digital-object link in any of the **24** tested disk and DVD rows. [Official finding aid, boxes 16 and 18](https://www.archives.gov/research/foia/faa-finding-aid-12-23)
+
+The 2001 and 2003 custody lists for **ORB #180** separately preserve **Safe** and **Litigation Drawer** location fields. The accession inventory supplies a later archival description, with **N90-7** and **N90-187** as separate identifiers. The prior July 2004 estimate named Atlantic City Technical Center as the required copying location. A checkout, duplication or return record with an item number and date would test the connection between the estimate and the separately listed DVD. The record of any physical movement remains open. [Regional estimate and custody rows](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/6cb41100f9300b81718e961493e77b729640f8c7/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-n90-national-foia-response-2026-11-09/README.md) · [Archive accession inventory](https://www.archives.gov/files/faa-inventory.pdf#page=52)
+
+## A literal endpoint shared by two records
+
+**N90-9** and **N90-189** both give the literal endpoint **63UTC** after **1308 UTC** for **ORB #4**. It appears in the PDF page images and the HTML finding aid. The row remains a description-level match by the printed tokens. **63UTC** remains unparsed as a time. The original label or recording metadata would test what that string represents. PDF default extraction also inserts a space in **ORB # 180** at physical p. 56 line 87, while the p. 56 image and HTML row read **ORB #180**. The image, HTML and extraction locators stay separate. [ORB #4 disk row](https://www.archives.gov/files/faa-inventory.pdf#page=52) · [DVD rows](https://www.archives.gov/files/faa-inventory.pdf#page=57) · [Exact stored fields](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## Shipping and certification access
+
+Box **15** catalogs **N90-285**, **N90-286**, **N90-287** and **N90-289** as airbill or related index/list records. The N90-286 title refers to a **10-15-2003** certified index memo. The N90-289 title refers to a **10-8-2003** custody list. Those are title fields. The rendered N90-286 record showed a PDF download link and **Access: Possibly Restricted**. The four direct catalog-linked media responses separately returned **200 / text/html**, **5,454 bytes** each, with identical SHA-256. Those responses contained empty catalog app roots. The shipping and certification bodies and any item-level link to #180 remain unacquired. [N90-285](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34915741) · [N90-286](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34915743) · [N90-287](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34915745) · [N90-289](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34915747)
+
+The repeatable check pinned the exact official HTML and 557-page inventory PDF, verified **24** finding-aid rows and **17** selected PDF text anchors, and visually checked the cited disk and DVD rows. It also verified four catalog records, four response bodies and the rendered N90-286 snapshot. The original media, executed Technical Center job, shipping receipt, final FOIA responses and FAA correction and signed disposition remain open. [Sources, verification and open inputs](SOURCE-PINS.json) · [Text addition](TEXT-CHANGES.diff)
